# Line-ending policy (docs/22 T0b, 2026-11-03).
#
# Why: this repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Windows
# checkouts therefore carried CRLF into SQL migration files, and
# `prisma migrate deploy` stores the migration text verbatim inside plpgsql
# function bodies. A database migrated on Windows then differed from the same
# database migrated in CI (Linux) — cosmetic for plpgsql, but it makes
# `pg_dump --schema-only` comparisons noisy and turns an environment
# difference into permanent schema drift.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: only SQL (migrations, provisioning scripts).
# Normalising every file type is a separate decision with its own review cost.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by bash (CI, and a developer reproducing the E2E
# stack locally). A CRLF checkout turns `set -euo pipefail` into a syntax error
# and the shebang into an unknown interpreter, so their bytes must be LF even on
# a Windows working copy with core.autocrlf=true.
*.sh text eol=lf
